WEBVTT

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.930
Stronghold of Lust

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.310
<Where is Pleguzes Jiart?>

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.510
<You may begin.>

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.060
<Your Majesty!>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.910
To see the oracle's prophecy fulfilled,

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.490
we have conducted multiple
reconnaissance missions.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.910
I believe it is now time
to launch a massive strike.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.670
I'd love to hear how you
came to that conclusion!

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.090
I hope that this encompassing strike
is not a waste of time, Dolgana.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.740
Naturally, there is no
point in making such

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:33.390
a maneuver if it fails to
usher staggering results.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.550
It would seem that some of the primitives
are capable of flying like us.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.470
You mean the ones who kicked your butt?

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.850
I-if I had more time, I could have
turned them into a sea of blood!

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.550
That is enough!

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.700
Dolgana, let us hear your plan.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.430
Your Majesty!

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.030
For starters, I would like
Klein to fight in the vanguard.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:54.660
Cool!

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.990
We will follow behind and
hunt down the lamata!

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.690
Very well.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.260
What would you have me do?

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.780
Babysit Lumes?

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:06.950
Lutiel, I would like you and Lumes
to finish off the remaining lamata.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.890
Dolgana, you will be in
charge of this Ta Hevara.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.660
Your Majesty!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.640
May the gods be with you!

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.490
How does everyone find working together
for the shikaara amusing?

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.220
I've heard that this journey's prophecy

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.310
is of a scale that comes
only once every 300 years.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.020
The lamata have resisted beyond our-

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.160
The thrill of the hunt comes from everyone
relying upon their own skills!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.370
At any rate, I'm going
to put this to an end.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.830
The impatient brat!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.740
May I have a glass?

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.860
You're still here, Lutiel?

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.760
This wine is most delicious.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:10.690
Shouldn't you see to your preparations?

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:13.170
I'll leave after one more glass.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.140
I'm quite excited!

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.770
What will I get to mount in my manor
after this Ta Hevara?

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.160
This prophecy is not meant
for your personal gain.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.550
Bear that in mind.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.750
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.640
Take care of it.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:23.260
Your Highness!

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.780
Pleguzes!

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.720
The parisada just adjourned
a few minutes ago.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.740
I am aware.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.700
Then where were you?!

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:37.940
Jiart!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:41.280
Brother...

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.070
You are hurt.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.350
Tend to him.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.340
I would have appreciated
your attendance, Pleguzes.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.290
That is enough.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.200
But Your Majesty-!

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.440
You cannot measure him by

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.250
your set of standards, not my brother.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.300
Brother, would you care for a match?

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.260
I must prepare for Ta Hevara.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.690
Purify yourself and prepare for battle.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.030
I can smell my brother on you...

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.790
Pleguzes?

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.330
Accept your fate!

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.020
Prince Jiart!

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.000
Move!

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.000
My!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.500
Is it to your liking?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.810
I like how it is more humble than you.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:08.450
My brother's woman was also humble.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.330
And she was not to your liking?

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.960
It made her boring.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:19.120
Even I may not amply satisfy you,
Prince Pleguzes.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.600
You are the very image of a Manaava.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:27.130
You obey your instincts
as you obtain anything you desire.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.510
Instinct...

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.640
But those lamata!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.440
Supposedly they consider
it a disgrace to obey

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.520
one's instinct and drown in desire.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:41.260
But isn't there dignity in
the instinct of the living?

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.280
Take what you want.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.160
Kill those you wish to kill.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.270
And rape those you wish to rape,

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.740
yes, Pleguzes Jiart?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:59.330
Do you think that race of lamata
can defy our instincts?

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:06.520
So? Why exactly are we implementing
this kind of operation?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.000
As I already explained,

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.860
we were successfully able to
shrink the light wave weapon.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.340
However, it takes time to fire.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.190
Furthermore, it is unable
to fire a chain of shots.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:17.650
As such, we must rely on tactics that-

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.000
Got it, got it.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.650
S-sir, I wasn't done yet!

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.520
I can figure out the rest from there.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:24.270
Now, more importantly!

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.490
Could anything use some sprucing up?

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.480
Sir?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.750
How do I look?

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.240
Commander in Chief Zorig of the GDF

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.340
will explain the situation
leading to the present.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:50.340
Our GDF army was originally formed
as a space security force.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.390
The economic powers of the world
established their own armies.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:56.200
And those armies were unified as one,
becoming the GDF.

00:08:56.650 --> 00:09:00.820
Afterwards, the Wulgaru hit us
with a surprise attack.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.360
As it was our first encounter
with foes from outer space,

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.900
it was difficult for us to respond
in a unified manner.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:10.670
However, we've finally reached

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:15.740
the point where we are capable
of full-scale operations.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.910
Upon multiple analyses primarily

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.650
conducted by the Operations Command,

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.930
we have completed what we believe to be

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.850
the best strategy for this upcoming battle.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.410
We consider it imperative that

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:32.510
the media and the people of
the world offer their support.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:36.640
As such, we would like to disclose
the content of our strategy in detail.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.310
If you would, Vice
Chief of Staff Komine.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.010
Sir!

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.810
Huh? Lt. Amane, what are you doing here?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.070
Why can't I be here?

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.820
Isn't it almost time for you to explain
the strategy to the media?

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.040
Weren't you were the central figure
behind devising this plan?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:54.820
Look.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:02.830
Allow me to explain our strategy.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.250
The GDF's recent assault on

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.870
the enemy base on Planetoid
RA221 ended in success.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.840
However, we believe that the enemy
is preparing to retaliate.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.880
As such, we have decided
to destroy Ragazza,

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.480
the enemy's frontline base,

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:22.070
which is located in close proximity
to our army base on Ceres.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.950
First we will attack

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:30.220
the enemy with our
cutting-edge laser-based system.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.440
To prevent the enemy from rushing us,
we will set up a minefield.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:38.010
On top of that, the mobile troops will

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.700
fire in unison with disposable rail guns.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:43.450
After that, we will enter normal battle.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:45.730
Having predicted the enemy's path,

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.830
we have positioned vessels in front of Ceres

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.120
that will fire a volley of guided

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.370
sublight speed guns and
free electron cannons.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.280
Afterwards, we will focus
on absolute defense

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:56.170
until the light wave weapon is fully charged.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:59.770
Once the heavy tactical
laser has charged,

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.140
the vanguard mobile troops
and vessels will leave

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.770
the laser's line of fire.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:06.970
Upon evacuation, we will destroy the

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.440
Wulgaru base along with their fleet!

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:12.690
That is all!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.350
With this, the Battle of Ceres,

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:18.540
the GDF will do everything within
its power to win this war!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.670
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.340
Let me introduce her.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:30.680
She will be in charge of
managing your schedules,

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:31.900
Miss Peko Yamada.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.590
It's a pleasure!

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:35.890
Th-the pleasure's mine.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.390
She is boarding the mother ship with us.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:42.260
I'll be supervising your schedules
and everyday lives.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:45.350
If you run into any difficulties
in your work or daily lives,

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.450
please feel free to
come see me for advice!

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.110
I'll even give you tips on love!

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:52.560
In that case, I could
use some personal advi-

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.990
Please look after them.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.200
Sure, Captain!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:00.780
Excuse me!

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.160
Yes?

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.360
Um, what should we do?

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:07.200
Are we supposed to participate
in that Battle of Ceres

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.730
they just announced?

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.880
Yes, but you'll be on
standby for a while first.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.720
S-standby?

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.420
You're free to do as
you like on Star Rose.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.760
Now I have a meeting to attend.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.230
Shall we get going?

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:26.860
I've prepared new rooms
for everyone on Star Rose.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:32.850
Here!

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.200
You can also use it for purchases
in the mess hall and at kiosks.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:39.710
Please let me know if
you need anything else.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.710
Well, take care!

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:42.860
Uh, thanks.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.160
Everyone gets their own room, huh?

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.920
This is mine!

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.960
Awesome!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.220
It's like a VIP room...

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.000
It's so different from the dorm!

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:12.270
Everyone, go to your own room!

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.230
I-I guess we should.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.670
Let's go to our rooms.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.370
So what are all of you doing in my room?

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:25.580
Well, uh, it felt right...

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.370
My room gives me the willies.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.410
These rooms are too big
for just one person.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.830
Wanna live together?

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.960
Wh-why don't we check out the mess hall?

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:40.540
They have curry!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.250
Excuse me! Do you have
pickled fish guts?

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:45.200
I'm going back to my room.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.090
I'm not terribly hungry, either.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:48.680
Sorry.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.860
Izurucchi!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.390
Why doncha join us?

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.540
Would you like something?
I'll get it for you.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.730
I'd recommend the
yakiniku meal for today.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.740
Th-then I'll have that.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:03.710
Just hang tight!

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:04.820
Thanks!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:05.660
Your schooling.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:06.660
Huh?

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.460
I heard you graduated.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.240
Uh, right.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:10.690
Congrats!

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:12.590
Yeah...

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:14.950
You don't seem too happy about it.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:17.420
It happened so fast.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.860
And now I don't have
a home to return to.

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:20.790
Thanks for waiting!

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.130
But aren't you going to come back
here from now on?

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.010
Just think of us as your family!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:27.480
Family...?

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.600
We're something like family.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.060
Be sure to return,

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.310
Be sure to return,
once you've taken off in flight,

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:32.300
Be sure to return,
once you've taken off in flight,
Migratory Bird.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.610
You don't have to respond to that.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:40.990
Y-you see, I don't have any
memories of my family,

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:43.330
so I'm not sure what it's like.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.110
But supposedly I had foster
parents for a while...

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.760
You'll find out what it's like.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:52.750
It's been a long time
since I left the nest.

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.880
Now this vessel feels like home.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:59.090
I think of Degawa as my father and
Dan as my older brother.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:01.250
Okay...

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:03.680
What's wrong?

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:06.640
Well, heroes are supposed to be loners.

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:07.720
What?

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:11.980
Finish eating?

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.230
Y-yeah.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.270
Is something the matter?

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:15.760
It doesn't feel like I ate.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.650
The Battle of Ceres is
disconcerting, isn't it?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:20.360
There's that, too.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:22.900
But my pit crew also wanted to talk.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.940
I couldn't relax.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:24.930
Say what?!

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.430
You're doing better
with yours than I am mine!

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.900
Totally! You've got it good!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.120
I wanna swap with Kei!

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.820
Isn't Kei's crew filled with hot babes?

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:32.920
Not again...

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.040
Compared to that, mine's filled with...

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:41.500
And mine...

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.000
Ah ♪

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:46.590
My crew seems like it
was originally a family.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.700
They even have a kid.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.520
If this is where we're
permanently stationed,

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.520
do you think they'll want to talk every day?

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:58.650
It must be rough having a family.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:01.520
That just made me feel a bit better!

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.030
Why?

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:07.320
Not having a family might actually
make life pretty carefree, huh?

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:16.230
Indeed.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.580
So why is everyone in my room?!

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:24.610
I'm going to copy this.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.170
F-fine...

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:33.800
What are you doing?!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:38.170
This ain't the place for
manga-drawing brats!

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.280
How did you sneak in here?

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.110
Uh, well, ummm...

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:42.520
Hey!

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:44.910
What's going on here?

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:45.780
We'll help you out!

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.690
Are you making fun of our pilot?

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.790
He is doing a splendid
job fighting the enemy!

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:55.080
He's the one out there protecting us!

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.080
Let's go!

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:57.870
Damn!

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.130
Th-thank you very much!

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:03.140
There's no need to thank us.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.150
It's no big.

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:05.330
You're awesome!

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.470
Izuru, you can really draw!

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.310
Make me the hero in your next piece!

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:12.480
This is great!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:15.770
Heroes with families
can be nice too, huh?

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:16.720
What?

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.360
This is Godinion.
Requesting permission for takeoff.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:24.150
This is control.
Godinion is cleared for takeoff.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.780
Cleared for takeoff. All ranges: Green.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:27.450
Increasing backup engine output.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:28.570
Before start check: Complete.
Increasing backup engine output.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:28.740
Before start check: Complete.
External power has been established.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:28.910
Disconnect all equipment.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:29.900
Start all engines!
Disconnect all equipment.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.910
Internal pressure increasing.
Turbines activated.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:34.240
Main engine military!

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:35.400
Blast off!

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:50.220
You've checked their heavy armament,
exchanged malfunctioning parts

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:53.640
and swapped anything that has
given any errors, right?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.940
They just need one last fine tuning.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:03.030
The Battle of Ceres is our
first big battle, isn't it?

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.540
That's true for the AHSMB, too.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.410
I hope the AHSMB units
don't decide to turn tail and run.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.780
The JURIA-SYSTEM...

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.040
It's insane how much it improves
the machine's response time,

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:16.250
but it's extremely difficult to control.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.150
It's an amazing yet annoying system.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:21.450
If it responds too strongly
to the pilot, it falls apart!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:27.210
I imagine we'll use their full armament
and pit crews for this battle.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:30.220
This reminds me of the F1's crew...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:31.850
Leave them to me!

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.420
We've been working on how to repair

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.950
the AHSMB while they're
in the midst of battle.

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:35.680
What?!

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:39.240
Everyone in the pit crews
will offer their full support!

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:20.970
Pleguzes Jiart, thank you
for your participation.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.270
I swear that we will protect you.

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:27.530
I do not need your protection.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:29.320
I have no intention of
participating in the shikaara.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.570
I am here only here in
case Teoria shows herself.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.270
Pleguzesia...

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.630
That which I want never
falls within my grasp!

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:43.240
It drives my lusts and
stimulates my instincts!

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:03.810
Isn't this pretty close to Ceres?

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:04.810
Yeah.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.480
When are we gonna sortie?

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:09.220
Once we get the orders.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.030
When'll that be?!

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.200
Pipe down!

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.660
Come to think of it, where's Suruga?

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.570
Awesome!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.450
On top of the usual fare,
I've got massive anti-ship guided missiles,

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:23.120
high-mobility guided missiles
and a midrange impact cannon!

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:26.040
You may be strappin' tough guns,
but you're still squishy.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.630
Let's do push-ups together
until it's time to sortie!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:32.890
Sweating with guys
just isn't my thing...

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:33.930
What?!

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.040
Th-that aside, can I
glue this on somewhere?

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.550
All AHSMB pilots, board your units!

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.230
Prepare to sortie! Please!

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.570
Once you've boarded,
wait there until further notice.

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:54.660
Uh, okay!

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.320
Do your best to remain calm.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:21:00.270
If you shrink from battle,
the AHSMBs will focus on defense.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:02.950
Let's do our best, Asagicchi!

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:05.120
Huh? Why the heck did you call me that?

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.770
Izuru was trying to help
you loosen up, Asagi.

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:11.620
Izuru!

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.260
I'll do my best to become a hero.

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:25.160
The goal behind DNA is to survive
and create copies of itself.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:29.190
The JURIA-SYSTEM awakens
various instincts.

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:33.680
Consequentially, it horribly
shakes the pilot's heart.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.110
Operation commences in T-30 minutes.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:43.410
Enemy vessels at Point Tango!

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:44.070
What?!

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.210
The enemy is attacking our
primary line of defense!

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:47.530
They out-maneuvered us!

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.300
Fire your railgun!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:55.090
It's too late!
Fire your railgun!

00:21:57.430 --> 00:22:00.260
We've lost 70% of the
1st Mobile Strike Force.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:01.260
Then fight back!

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:02.720
Please wait! We aren't ready to-

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.210
I can't! Commence the attack!

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.670
We're starting?!

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:55.910
Battle of Ceres
